-- Oracle for the two @desc-attachment rules `L4.Parser.ResolveAnnotation`
-- implements. Both were, at different times, silently wrong: `instance HasDesc
-- (Expr n)` was `pure`, so the desc pass never descended into an expression at
-- all, and its first repair descended only into a `WHERE`/`LET` sitting at the
-- top of a body. In every failing case `l4 check` reported success and the
-- annotation simply vanished, which is why this file exists.
--
--   1. A @desc written above a WHERE binding is claimed by THAT BINDING, and
--      not left pending for a later top-level declaration to claim
--      (`descPrecedesNode` admits any preceding desc within 8 columns of
--      slack, so "a later declaration claims it" is the real alternative, not
--      a hypothetical one). Read off the `auto terms:` glossary, which keys
--      every entry by the name of the definition that owns the gloss.
--
--   2. A @desc written above a LET binding NESTED INSIDE another expression is
--      claimed by that binding too. Read off `l4 ast`: the glossary cannot see
--      this one, because `collectGlossary` walks only a WHERE/LET at the top
--      of a decide body.

@desc A parcel of land
DECLARE Parcel
    HAS
      @desc whether the parcel is registered
      `registered` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Land Titles Act s 4
@export Whether the parcel may be transferred
GIVEN p IS A Parcel @desc The parcel under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `transfer permitted` p IF `title is clean`
 WHERE
    @desc BINDINGGLOSS the title is free of encumbrance
    `title is clean` MEANS p's `registered`

-- Deliberately carries NO @desc of its own: if the binding gloss above were
-- still pending when the desc pass reached here, THIS is what would claim it,
-- and the glossary would key that text under `claim window in days`.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `claim window in days` IS
    IF TRUE
    THEN LET
           @desc NESTEDGLOSS a LET binding inside an IF arm
           `grace period` BE 14
         IN `grace period`
    ELSE 0

#EVAL `transfer permitted` OF Parcel WITH `registered` IS TRUE
-- TRUE

#EVAL `claim window in days`
-- 14
